om/users/louistrue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louistrue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louistrue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louistrue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louistrue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/louistrue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LTplus-AG/NHMzh-plugin-qto/commits/959c7f1d4f5e1d76d1c1e82dc97ae90bb6f49306/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-26T08:15:51Z","email":"78563314+louistrue@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Louis Trümpler"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-26T08:15:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: update element identifier in API client and related components (#44)\n\n* fix: update element identifier in API client and related components\n\n- Changed `element_id` to `global_id` in the API client and associated types for consistency.\n- Updated references in the MainPage component to reflect the new identifier.\n- Updated package-lock.json for caniuse-lite version bump and added license information.\n\n* refactor: update quantity handling in API client and components\n\n- Introduced a new `QuantityData` interface to standardize quantity representation.\n- Updated `ElementQuantityUpdate` type to use the new `QuantityData` structure.\n- Refactored `approveProjectElements` method to streamline quantity updates.\n- Enhanced type assertions in `MainPage` component for better validation of quantity types.\n- Added logging for skipped updates due to missing or invalid quantity types.\n\n* refactor: deprecate approveProjectElements method and enhance quantity type handling\n\n- Marked the `approveProjectElements` method as deprecated, recommending the use of `approveProject()` for future implementations.\n- Updated `QuantityType` to include \"count\" for better representation of quantities.\n- Enhanced type validation in the `MainPage` component to ensure only valid quantity types are processed, improving robustness and logging for unsupported types.\n\n* refactor: improve quantity type handling in MainPage component\n\n- Simplified quantity type validation by using an array to check valid types.\n- Enhanced unit assignment logic for quantities based on their type, ensuring appropriate default units are used for area, volume, length, and count.\n\n* refactor: add type guard for quantity type validation\n\n- Introduced a type guard function `isQuantityType` to streamline validation of quantity types in the MainPage component.\n- Replaced manual type checks with the new type guard for improved readability and maintainability.\n- Enhanced unit assignment logic to ensure correct default units are applied based on quantity type.\n\n* refactor: enhance project approval logging and update database schema\n\n- Improved logging during project approval to include detailed information about quantity updates and element states before and after approval.\n- Added a new index for `global_id` in the MongoDB schema to optimize queries related to element updates.\n- Updated README to reflect changes in the frontend build process and added Vite as a bundler.\n- Adjusted TypeScript version in README badges for accuracy.\n\n* refactor: clean up comments and enhance API client interfaces\n\n- Removed outdated comment markers and improved clarity in the `ApiClient.ts` file.\n- Updated the `ClassificationData` and `ProjectMetadata` interfaces for better readability.\n- Deprecated the `approveProjectElements` method, consolidating functionality into `approveProject`.\n- Enhanced the `batchUpdateElements`, `getTargetIfcClasses`, and `deleteElement` methods with clearer comments.\n\n* refactor: enhance logging format and improve error handling in backend\n\n- Updated logging statements across multiple files to use structured formatting for better readability and consistency.\n- Improved error handling in MongoDB operations and IFC processing functions to provide clearer context in logs.\n- Refactored material fraction normalization logging in `ifc_materials_parser.py` for better clarity.\n- Enhanced type assertions and error messages in the `MainPage` component for improved debugging.\n\n* refactor: standardize volume handling across components\n\n- Introduced a new helper function `getVolumeValue` to streamline volume extraction from various formats (number or object).\n- Updated volume calculations in `ExcelImportDialog`, `MainPage`, `MaterialsTable`, and other components to utilize the new helper for consistency.\n- Adjusted type definitions in `types.ts` to accommodate volume as an object with optional properties.\n- Enhanced zero quantity checks to leverage the new volume handling logic.","tree":{"sha":"c22029a74b1579055b9f764742377779af8c4563","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LTplus-AG/NHMzh-plugin-qto/git/trees/c22029a74b1579055b9f764742377779af8c4563"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LTplus-AG/NHMzh-plugin-qto/git/commits/959c7f1d4f5e1d76d1c1e82dc97ae90bb6f49306","verification":{"payload":"tree c22029a74b1579055b9f764742377779af8c4563\nparent 83ec5ad446529060d5422b2e8b37923e2177e571\nauthor Louis Trümpler <78563314+louistrue@users.noreply.github.com> 1761466551 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1761466551 +0100\n\nfix: update element identifier in API client and related components (#44)\n\n* fix: update element identifier in API client and related components\n\n- Changed `element_id` to `global_id` in the API client and associated types for consistency.\n- Updated references in the MainPage component to reflect the new identifier.\n- Updated package-lock.json for caniuse-lite version bump and added license information.\n\n* refactor: update quantity handling in API client and components\n\n- Introduced a new `QuantityData` interface to standardize quantity representation.\n- Updated `ElementQuantityUpdate` type to use the new `QuantityData` structure.\n- Refactored `approveProjectElements` method to streamline quantity updates.\n- Enhanced type assertions in `MainPage` component for better validation of quantity types.\n- Added logging for skipped updates due to missing or invalid quantity types.\n\n* refactor: deprecate approveProjectElements method and enhance quantity type handling\n\n- Marked the `approveProjectElements` method as deprecated, recommending the use of `approveProject()` for future implementations.\n- Updated `QuantityType` to include \"count\" for better representation of quantities.\n- Enhanced type validation in the `MainPage` component to ensure only valid quantity types are processed, improving robustness and logging for unsupported types.\n\n* refactor: improve quantity type handling in MainPage component\n\n- Simplified quantity type validation by using an array to check valid types.\n- Enhanced unit assignment logic for quantities based on their type, ensuring appropriate default units are used for area, volume, length, and count.\n\n* refactor: add type guard for quantity type validation\n\n- Introduced a type guard function `isQuantityType` to streamline validation of quantity types in the MainPage component.\n- Replaced manual type checks with the new type guard for improved readability and maintainability.\n- Enhanced unit assignment logic to ensure correct default units are applied based on quantity type.\n\n* refactor: enhance project approval logging and update database schema\n\n- Improved logging during project approval to include detailed information about quantity updates and element states before and after approval.\n- Added a new index for `global_id` in the MongoDB schema to optimize queries related to element updates.\n- Updated README to reflect changes in the frontend build process and added Vite as a bundler.\n- Adjusted TypeScript version in README badges for accuracy.\n\n* refactor: clean up comments and enhance API client interfaces\n\n- Removed outdated comment markers and improved clarity in the `ApiClient.ts` file.\n- Updated the `ClassificationData` and `ProjectMetadata` interfaces for better readability.\n- Deprecated the `approveProjectElements` method, consolidating functionality into `approveProject`.\n- Enhanced the `batchUpdateElements`, `getTargetIfcClasses`, and `deleteElement` methods with clearer comments.\n\n* refactor: enhance logging format and improve error handling in backend\n\n- Updated logging statements across multiple files to use structured formatting for better readability and consistency.\n- Improved error handling in MongoDB operations and IFC processing functions to provide clearer context in logs.\n- Refactored material fraction normalization logging in `ifc_materials_parser.py` for better clarity.\n- Enhanced type assertions and error messages in the `MainPage` component for improved debugging.\n\n* refactor: standardize volume handling across components\n\n- Introduced a new helper function `getVolumeValue` to streamline volume extraction from various formats (number or object).\n- Updated volume calculations in `ExcelImportDialog`, `MainPage`, `MaterialsTable`, and other components to utilize the new helper for consistency.\n- Adjusted type definitions in `types.ts` to accommodate volume as an object with optional properties.\n- Enhanced zero quantity checks to leverage the new volume handling logic.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJo/di3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASL4QAKHuzzQVhCF2O+iHaSP4EEoa\ntEaix9JjA3oRsL+NM2+XjHJ2cv9C9nA/PEZss7IP1PB2lB3OaPCFhz43ERHs4H5F\npAJeX+3qWW4CIs/Cp9z7aXQCjvOb17z3zCjrhLEztahlqYjPI0Crl6HzhfkSOZYd\n/a2oghOj+CO9SkJe7pBWHDstIBHr0MTLhnoG1J9kkZb33YFmI9vJ3xxmngMYJvn1\nZ1oBdguKOTvit6945Et/a4knaO1PwXAeD97zSERiOc3faNTtfxf0pJqiRuAqCfG1\nzj+p6prwkI4VitPlabsbYVFlFEyeEP7MBnrcmdTfkzny2CC18NFoSZ0a7laJvYHT\niWu6TBlciGoPTIXdRQZ6F3oPwSafngwh6D1d30195r9RtL7ozcV9Pzh+z3ZjdQLO\nDC6ljVPTSKRMelb/AspnHmJTAfd