tps://github.com/nishiegroe/NishieGroePersonalWebsite/commit/29d55026c0be51f26bfec126cf0b01c4f82738fc","sha":"29d55026c0be51f26bfec126cf0b01c4f82738fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nishiegroe/NishieGroePersonalWebsite/commits/29d55026c0be51f26bfec126cf0b01c4f82738fc"}],"sha":"3e44474a386c688e20e05ad2981230e54b92d4db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nishiegroe/NishieGroePersonalWebsite/commits/3e44474a386c688e20e05ad2981230e54b92d4db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10037605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishiegroe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishiegroe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishiegroe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishiegroe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nishiegroe","id":10037605,"login":"nishiegroe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDM3NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishiegroe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishiegroe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishiegroe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishiegroe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishiegroe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nishiegroe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nishiegroe/NishieGroePersonalWebsite/commits/29d55026c0be51f26bfec126cf0b01c4f82738fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-20T20:07:41Z","email":"nishiegroe@gmail.com","name":"Nishie Groe"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-20T20:07:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Modern Feminine Portfolio Redesign (#15)\n\n* Add Featured Projects section to showcase VOD Insights\n\n- Create new Projects component with project cards displaying:\n  - Project title, description, key features\n  - Technology stack as badges\n  - Links to website and GitHub\n  - Screenshot support\n- Add VOD Insights as primary featured project\n- Update App.tsx to include Projects between Skills and Employment History\n- Add Projects link to mobile navigation menu\n- Include VOD Insights home page screenshot in public assets\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add Projects component to App.jsx (the actual entry point)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Redesign Projects component to match site aesthetic\n\n- Simplify layout: remove screenshot, focus on clean card design\n- Match Employment History styling: gray header with title/description\n- Use bullet points for key highlights instead of feature lists\n- Show tech stack as inline text\n- Add website link in header with consistent blue color scheme\n- Update section title to ''Projects'' (from ''Featured Projects'')\n- Improve readability and visual hierarchy\n- Reduce visual complexity for better integration with site design\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Redesign Projects to match Employment History structure\n\n- Wrap entire Projects section in Card container with constrained width (680px mobile, 960px desktop)\n- Left-align title ''Projects'' (centered on mobile) to match Employment History\n- Use ProjectEntry components matching EmploymentHistoryEntry structure\n- Add both VOD Insights and Lootpath Finder projects\n- Use colored headers for visual distinction between projects (blue and teal)\n- Align margins, padding, and styling to match Employment History exactly\n- Technology stack displayed in top right alongside website link\n- Key highlights shown as bullet points below header\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add project image showcase to Projects component\n\n- Add image property to ProjectEntry component\n- Display featured project screenshot centered between header and highlights\n- Image has max height of 300px with rounded corners and light background\n- VOD Insights now shows application home page screenshot\n- Supports image alt text for accessibility\n- Lootpath Finder ready for image addition (no screenshot available yet)\n- Outer card structure unchanged, only inner content enhanced\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add image gallery feature to Projects component\n\n- Support multiple images per project with carousel functionality\n- Add prev/next navigation arrows for browsing images\n- Add clickable gallery dots to jump to specific images\n- Display image counter (dots indicator) below gallery\n- Add 4 VOD Insights screenshots:\n  - Home page (VOD library view)\n  - Clips page (exported clips browser)\n  - VOD Viewer page (analysis interface)\n  - Clip Viewer page (clip creation interface)\n- Gallery navigation is keyboard and mouse accessible\n- Dots change color (blue) to show current image\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add Lootpath Finder screenshots to Projects gallery\n\n- Add 3 Lootpath Finder screenshots to image gallery:\n  - Home page (map selection interface)\n  - Map editor example\n  - Lootpath example\n- Rename screenshot files for consistency (spaces to hyphens)\n- Lootpath Finder now has full carousel gallery with prev/next navigation\n- Gallery dots support quick navigation between images\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add configurable accent color system and UI/UX enhancements\n\n**Theme System:**\n- Create centralized theme configuration (src/theme/colors.ts)\n- Add theme hook for dynamic CSS variable injection (src/theme/useTheme.ts)\n- Implement comprehensive CSS variables for all colors\n- Support easy accent color changes in one place\n\n**UI/UX Improvements:**\n- Enhanced global styles with smooth transitions\n- Improved card hover effects with subtle lift animation\n- Better focus states for accessibility\n- Smooth link underline animations\n- Refined button interactions\n- Better form element styling\n- Staggered animation support for lists\n\n**Design Polish:**\n- Consistent animation timing via CSS variables\n- Improved scrollbar styling\n- Better selection styling\n- Refined transitions on interactive elements\n- Enhanced color palette with light/hover/active states\n\n**Documentation:**\n- Add THEME_GUIDE.md with preset color options\n- Include instructions for changing accent color\n- Provide examples of dynamic theming\n- Document all CSS variables and customization options\n\nColors included:\n- Blue (current): #36c0f0\n- Indigo: #6366f1\n- Cyan: #00d4ff\n- Pink: #ec4899\n- Emerald: #10b981\n- Orange: #f97316\n- Violet: #8b5cf6\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update theme palette to Modern Feminine aesthetic\n\nChanged accent color from bright blue (#36c0f0) to warm lavender (#d9a8c7)\nwith peachy rose accents (#f5b8a8). Updated background to soft cream (#faf8f5)\nand text colors to warm earth tones for a cohesive, elegant feminine design.\n\nColor updates:\n- Accent: #d9a8c7 (warm lavender)\n- Accent light: rgba(245, 184, 168, 0.1)\n- Accent hover: #c697b8\n- Background: #faf8f5 (soft cream)\n- Text primary: #3a3531 (warm brown)\n- Text secondary: #7a7066 (warm taupe)\n- Border: #ede8e0 (warm beige)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve responsive design and add scroll snap behavior\n\nChanges:\n- Fixed skill hover glow from blue to warm lavender (rgba(217, 168, 199, 0.6))\n- Improved project card responsive design:\n  * Better spacing on desktop (2.5rem gap for 1024px+ screens)\n  * Increased card padding on desktop (2.5rem)\n  * Larger project images (350px at 768px, 400px at 1024px)\n  * Added flexbox layout for better content distribution\n- Added scroll snap behavior:\n  * scroll-snap-type: y mandatory on html\n  * scroll-snap-align: center and scroll-snap-stop: always on sections\n  * Smooth scrolling for better user experience\n  * Hero and all spatial sections now snap to center on scroll\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Implement automatic section jumping on scroll\n\nAdded smooth section navigation that jumps directly to next/previous section\non mouse wheel scroll, creating a polished full-page navigation experience.\n\nChanges:\n- Added scroll wheel event listener to detect scroll direction\n- Automatically finds current section and jumps to adjacent section\n- 1 second delay between jumps prevents rapid scrolling\n- Smooth scrolling animation centers sections in viewport\n- Removed CSS scroll-snap in favor of JavaScript control for better UX\n- Supports scrolling up and down through all sections\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Hide scrollbars for cleaner aesthetic\n\nRemoved visible scrollbars while maintaining full scroll functionality.\nUses CSS properties to hide scrollbars across all browsers:\n- scrollbar-width: none for Firefox\n- -ms-overflow-style: none for IE/Edge\n- ::-webkit-scrollbar display: none for Chrome/Safari\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Completely hide all scrollbars across all CSS files\n\nRemoved scrollbar styling from global.css and redesign.css to ensure\nno scrollbars are visible anywhere on the page. Set width/height to 0\nand display to none for webkit scrollbars.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Hide scrollbars on spatial-container element\n\nThe scrollbar was appearing on the .spatial-container div despite previous CSS rules. Added scrollbar-width: none, -ms-overflow-style: none, and ::-webkit-scrollbar rules specifically to this element to hide scrollbars across all browsers while maintaining scroll functionality and section jumping behavior.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Replace emoji icons with actual tech icons in skills constellation\n\nUpdated SkillsConstellation component to use developer-icons library instead of emoji characters. Added proper React component icons for React, TypeScript, Java, AWS, Node.js, PostgreSQL, Docker, Python, and Git for a more professional appearance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Expand skills constellation with all 21 skills grouped by category\n\nReorganized SkillsConstellation to display all available skills organized into 6 categories: Frontend (6), Backend (4), Database (3), DevOps (3), Testing (2), and Tools & CMS (3). Each skill shows its category on hover, and a color-coded legend below the constellation provides a visual guide for each skill type. Skills within the same category are positioned in clusters with stronger connection lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve skills constellation spacing and organization\n\nReorganized skill positions to spread categories across the full constellation area, eliminating overlapping and improving visual clarity. Frontend cluster now in top-left, Backend in top-right, Database in center, DevOps in bottom-left, Testing on right-middle, and Tools & CMS in bottom-center. Skills within categories maintain their groupings with stronger connection lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve skill label readability in constellation\n\nEnhanced label styling with white background, increased opacity, better positioning, and improved text contrast. Labels now display with a semi-transparent white background using backdrop blur, positioned below the skill icon, with the skill name and category clearly visible on hover. Updated skill-label CSS to remove opacity transitions and add background styling for better visibility.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Raise z-index of skill nodes and labels on hover\n\nAdded z-index: 100 to .skill-node:hover and z-index: 101 to .skill-node:hover .skill-label to ensure hovered skills and their labels appear above other elements in the constellation, preventing overlap issues and improving visibility.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve mobile scrolling experience\n\nDisabled automatic section jumping on mobile devices (viewport width < 768px) to allow natural scrolling without forced positioning interrupting readability. Changed desktop scrolling to use ''start'' positioning instead of ''center'' for better section visibility. Mobile users can now scroll smoothly without sections being forcibly centered and cutting off content at the bottom.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Completely disable section jumping on mobile for smooth scrolling\n\nRemoved all automatic section jumping on mobile devices (width < 768px) to provide a natural, uninterrupted scrolling experience. Mobile users can now scroll at their own pace without sections being forcibly repositioned. Desktop users (768px+) retain the smooth section-jumping navigation feature for a curated experience.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve section jumping algorithm to prevent backwards jumping\n\nChanged section detection from viewport center to viewport top for more reliable positioning. Added scroll direction tracking to prevent unintended backwards jumps when transitioning between sections. Increased scroll delay to 1200ms for smoother transitions. These changes prevent the ''jumping to previous section'' issue that occurred during transitions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Completely remove section jumping from mobile\n\nSimplified code to completely disable section jumping on mobile devices (width < 768px) by returning early from the useEffect. Mobile users now get pure natural scrolling with zero automatic section repositioning. Desktop users (768px+) retain the improved section jumping feature.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Make mobile sections full viewport height\n\nUpdated mobile responsive styles to set all sections (.spatial-section and .hero) to height: 100vh on mobile devices (max-width: 768px). Added flexbox centering to ensure content is properly centered vertically. This prevents the next section from being visible until the user scrolls to it, creating a cleaner mobile reading experience.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix mobile sections to expand when content exceeds viewport height\n\nChanged from fixed ''height: 100vh'' to ''min-height: 100vh'' on mobile sections. This allows sections to expand beyond the viewport when they contain more content than can fit, while keeping shorter sections at full viewport height. All project and experience content is now fully visible and scrollable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Replace social link text with logo icons in Contact section\n\n- Replace GitHub, LinkedIn, and Resume text labels with their respective logos\n- GitHub icon (#333 dark gray) from Material-UI\n- LinkedIn icon (#0077b5 standard LinkedIn blue) from Material-UI\n- Resume icon (DescriptionIcon in lavender #d9a8c7) from Material-UI\n- Icons maintain 32px size with hover opacity effects\n- All links maintain original functionality and accessibility (aria-labels)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Complete modern feminine portfolio redesign\n\nUpdates to multiple components and styles:\n- Hero section with smooth scroll-to-center navigation\n- Skills constellation with 25 technologies in 7 categories and internet logos\n- Improved contact section with logo icons\n- Responsive mobile and desktop layouts\n- Enhanced animations and visual styling\n- SEO improvements with hidden text and aria-labels\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b80ec6df91f10fb2808cb4c09b54d741a4788ca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nishiegroe/NishieGroePersonalWebsite/git/trees/b80ec6df91f10fb2808cb4c09b54d741a4788ca9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nishiegroe/NishieGroePersonalWebsite/git/commits/29d55026c0be51f26bfec126cf0b01c4f82738fc","verification":{"payload":"tree b80ec6df91f10fb2808cb4c09b54d741a4788ca9\nparent d276b051da03a5c2675912514d7ae3efad57f816\nauthor Nishie Groe <nishiegroe@gmail.com> 1774037261 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774037261 -0500\n\nModern Feminine Portfolio Redesign (#15)\n\n* Add Featured Projects section to showcase VOD Insights\n\n- Create new Projects component with project cards displaying:\n  - Project title, description, key features\n  - Technology stack as badges\n  - Links to website and GitHub\n  - Screenshot support\n- Add VOD Insights as primary featured project\n- Update App.tsx to include Projects between Skills and Employment History\n- Add Projects link to mobile navigation menu\n- Include VOD Insights home page screenshot in public assets\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add Projects component to App.jsx (the actual entry point)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Redesign Projects component to match site aesthetic\n\n- Simplify layout: remove screenshot, focus on clean card design\n- Match Employment History styling: gray header with title/description\n- Use bullet points for key highlights instead of feature lists\n- Show tech stack as inline text\n- Add website link in header with consistent blue color scheme\n- Update section title to ''Projects'' (from ''Featured Projects'')\n- Improve readability and visual hierarchy\n- Reduce visual complexity for better integration with site design\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Redesign Projects to match Employment History structure\n\n- Wrap entire Projects section in Card container with constrained width (680px mobile, 960px desktop)\n- Left-align title ''Projects'' (centered on mobile) to match Employment History\n- Use ProjectEntry components matching EmploymentHistoryEntry structure\n- Add both VOD Insights and Lootpath Finder projects\n- Use colored headers for visual distinction between projects (blue and teal)\n- Align margins, padding, and styling to match Employment History exactly\n- Technology stack displayed in top right alongside website link\n- Key highlights shown as bullet points below header\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add project image showcase to Projects component\n\n- Add image property to ProjectEntry component\n- Display featured project screenshot centered between header and highlights\n- Image has max height of 300px with rounded corners and light background\n- VOD Insights now shows application home page screenshot\n- Supports image alt text for accessibility\n- Lootpath Finder ready for image addition (no screenshot available yet)\n- Outer card structure unchanged, only inner content enhanced\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add image gallery feature to Projects component\n\n- Support multiple images per project with carousel functionality\n- Add prev/next navigation arrows for browsing images\n- Add clickable gallery dots to jump to specific images\n- Display image counter (dots indicator) below gallery\n- Add 4 VOD Insights screenshots:\n  - Home page (VOD library view)\n  - Clips page (exported clips browser)\n  - VOD Viewer page (analysis interface)\n  - Clip Viewer page (clip creation interface)\n- Gallery navigation is keyboard and mouse accessible\n- Dots change color (blue) to show current image\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add Lootpath Finder screenshots to Projects gallery\n\n- Add 3 Lootpath Finder screenshots to image gallery:\n  - Home page (map selection interface)\n  - Map editor example\n  - Lootpath example\n- Rename screenshot files for consistency (spaces to hyphens)\n- Lootpath Finder now has full carousel gallery with prev/next navigation\n- Gallery dots support quick navigation between images\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add configurable accent color system and UI/UX enhancements\n\n**Theme System:**\n- Create centralized theme configuration (src/theme/colors.ts)\n- Add theme hook for dynamic CSS variable injection (src/theme/useTheme.ts)\n- Implement comprehensive CSS variables for all colors\n- Support easy accent color changes in one place\n\n**UI/UX Improvements:**\n- Enhanced global styles with smooth transitions\n- Improved card hover effects with subtle lift animation\n- Better focus states for accessibility\n- Smooth link underline animations\n- Refined button interactions\n- Better form element styling\n- Staggered animation support for lists\n\n**Design Polish:**\n- Consistent animation timing via CSS variables\n- Improved scrollbar styling\n- Better selection styling\n- Refined transitions on interactive elements\n- Enhanced color palette with light/hover/active states\n\n**Documentation:**\n- Add THEME_GUIDE.md with preset color options\n- Include instructions for changing accent color\n- Provide examples of dynamic theming\n- Document all CSS variables and customization options\n\nColors included:\n- Blue (current): #36c0f0\n- Indigo: #6366f1\n- Cyan: #00d4ff\n- Pink: #ec4899\n- Emerald: #10b981\n- Orange: #f97316\n- Violet: #8b5cf6\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update theme palette to Modern Feminine aesthetic\n\nChanged accent color from bright blue (#36c0f0) to warm lavender (#d9a8c7)\nwith peachy rose accents (#f5b8a8). Updated background to soft cream (#faf8f5)\nand text colors to warm earth tones for a cohesive, elegant feminine design.\n\nColor updates:\n- Accent: #d9a8c7 (warm lavender)\n- Accent light: rgba(245, 184, 168, 0.1)\n- Accent hover: #c697b8\n- Background: #faf8f5 (soft cream)\n- Text primary: #3a3531 (warm brown)\n- Text secondary: #7a7066 (warm taupe)\n- Border: #ede8e0 (warm beige)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve responsive design and add scroll snap behavior\n\nChanges:\n- Fixed skill hover glow from blue to warm lavender (rgba(217, 168, 199, 0.6))\n- Improved project card responsive design:\n  * Better spacing on desktop (2.5rem gap for 1024px+ screens)\n  * Increased card padding on desktop (2.5rem)\n  * Larger project images (350px at 768px, 400px at 1024px)\n  * Added flexbox layout for better content distribution\n- Added scroll snap behavior:\n  * scroll-snap-type: y mandatory on html\n  * scroll-snap-align: center and scroll-snap-stop: always on sections\n  * Smooth scrolling for better user experience\n  * Hero and all spatial sections now snap to center on scroll\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Implement automatic section jumping on scroll\n\nAdded smooth section navigation that jumps directly to next/previous section\non mouse wheel scroll, creating a polished full-page navigation experience.\n\nChanges:\n- Added scroll wheel event listener to detect scroll direction\n- Automatically finds current section and jumps to adjacent section\n- 1 second delay between jumps prevents rapid scrolling\n- Smooth scrolling animation centers sections in viewport\n- Removed CSS scroll-snap in favor of JavaScript control for better UX\n- Supports scrolling up and down through all sections\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Hide scrollbars for cleaner aesthetic\n\nRemoved visible scrollbars while maintaining full scroll functionality.\nUses CSS properties to hide scrollbars across all browsers:\n- scrollbar-width: none for Firefox\n- -ms-overflow-style: none for IE/Edge\n- ::-webkit-scrollbar display: none for Chrome/Safari\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Completely hide all scrollbars across all CSS files\n\nRemoved scrollbar styling from global.css and redesign.css to ensure\nno scrollbars are visible anywhere on the page. Set width/height to 0\nand display to none for webkit scrollbars.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Hide scrollbars on spatial-container element\n\nThe scrollbar was appearing on the .spatial-container div despite previous CSS rules. Added scrollbar-width: none, -ms-overflow-style: none, and ::-webkit-scrollbar rules specifically to this element to hide scrollbars across all browsers while maintaining scroll functionality and section jumping behavior.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Replace emoji icons with actual tech icons in skills constellation\n\nUpdated SkillsConstellation component to use developer-icons library instead of emoji characters. Added proper React component icons for React, TypeScript, Java, AWS, Node.js, PostgreSQL, Docker, Python, and Git for a more professional appearance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Expand skills constellation with all 21 skills grouped by category\n\nReorganized SkillsConstellation to display all available skills organized into 6 categories: Frontend (6), Backend (4), Database (3), DevOps (3), Testing (2), and Tools & CMS (3). Each skill shows its category on hover, and a color-coded legend below the constellation provides a visual guide for each skill type. Skills within the same category are positioned in clusters with stronger connection lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve skills constellation spacing and organization\n\nReorganized skill positions to spread categories across the full constellation area, eliminating overlapping and improving visual clarity. Frontend cluster now in top-left, Backend in top-right, Database in center, DevOps in bottom-left, Testing on right-middle, and Tools & CMS in bottom-center. Skills within categories maintain their groupings with stronger connection lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve skill label readability in constellation\n\nEnhanced label styling with white background, increased opacity, better positioning, and improved text contrast. Labels now display with a semi-transparent white background using backdrop blur, positioned below the skill icon, with the skill name and category clearly visible on hover. Updated skill-label CSS to remove opacity transitions and add background styling for better visibility.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Raise z-index of skill nodes and labels on hover\n\nAdded z-index: 100 to .skill-node:hover and z-index: 101 to .skill-node:hover .skill-label to ensure hovered skills and their labels appear above other elements in the constellation, preventing overlap issues and improving visibility.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve mobile scrolling experience\n\nDisabled automatic section jumping on mobile devices (viewport width < 768px) to allow natural scrolling without forced positioning interrupting readability. Changed desktop scrolling to use ''start'' positioning instead of ''center'' for better section visibility. Mobile users can now scroll smoothly without sections being forcibly centered and cutting off content at the bottom.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Completely disable section jumping on mobile for smooth scrolling\n\nRemoved all automatic section jumping on mobile devices (width < 768px) to provide a natural, uninterrupted scrolling experience. Mobile users can now scroll at their own pace without sections being forcibly repositioned. Desktop users (768px+) retain the smooth section-jumping navigation feature for a curated experience.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve section jumping algorithm to prevent backwards jumping\n\nChanged section detection from viewport center to viewport top for more reliable positioning. Added scroll direction tracking to prevent unintended backwards jumps when transitioning between sections. Increased scroll delay to 1200ms for smoother transitions. These changes prevent the ''jumping to previous section'' issue that occurred during transitions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Completely remove section jumping from mobile\n\nSimplified code to completely disable section jumping on mobile devices (width < 768px) by returning early from the useEffect. Mobile users now get pure natural scrolling with zero automatic section repositioning. Desktop users (768px+) retain the improved section jumping feature.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Make mobile sections full viewport height\n\nUpdated mobile responsive styles to set all sections (.spatial-section and .hero) to height: 100vh on mobile devices (max-width: 768px). Added flexbox centering to ensure content is properly centered vertically. This prevents the next section from being visible until the user scrolls to it, creating a cleaner mobile reading experience.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix mobile sections to expand when content exceeds viewport height\n\nChanged from fixed ''height: 100vh'' to ''min-height: 100vh'' on mobile sections. This allows sections to expand beyond the viewport when they contain more content than can fit, while keeping shorter sections at full viewport height. All project and experience content is now fully visible and scrollable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Replace social link text with logo icons in Contact section\n\n- Replace GitHub, LinkedIn, and Resume text labels with their respective logos\n- GitHub icon (#333 dark gray) from Material-UI\n- LinkedIn icon (#0077b5 standard LinkedIn blue) from Material-UI\n- Resume icon (DescriptionIcon in lavender #d9a8c7) from Material-UI\n- Icons maintain 32px size with hover opacity effects\n- All links maintain original functionality and accessibility (aria-labels)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Complete modern feminine portfolio redesign\n\nUpdates to multiple components and styles:\n- Hero section with smooth scroll-to-center navigation\n- Skills constellation with 25 technologies in 7 categories and internet logos\n- Improved contact section with logo icons\n- Responsive mobile and desktop layouts\n- Enhanced animations and visual styling\n- SEO improvements with hidden text and aria-labels\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpvakNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz1cQADcHjaXBXnarsy71JGDm91Eu\nsLpJmOo9ROnV4HGVtBpXmusqsImEZcDOcA6OMGwc8f+Q6hhv2NAskiqqqwWr6v/B\ngmtU7N8q0EHGENwx+reKbRHHkvpRBLgmkkSoWPYgD869xcgjYqq+9UpUcJ1odfex\njxPIDB9gp9LkQvwBLCodYWbz3LHa+wba6tyzVRy8vM6huKbkDkc79C8z8+O6Ieoz\nSZ2zb/FiZhLtPw1DKkoQOMTF5OK8bbc33r4EhfADaz0M4Aa/gKjL8bwH48qYNj6u\nwmDdgkpBT6MF7WhBJZdMF1X5kTRFwitTGq0gRCZKYyLQP0eFt5v7aQIIk0ahGJDQ\n2FcO1zD6vNmUfiJ4bDPVJO3YsLRGStWg4QWGuixf6YYKJqRka+aR9eyJbLvembhS\nB34i3OX5dPvFihr5JL0ymi37KPiNoFNsnSvBRXAdxF6j/Yaf/Wr+LuDZxTf4ACVu\nCxY8yoURUD5Dkzgln3Y1CDooH9qrOaaZs8KA6I9oX8NVEKApLo3ax8xU23fzkyQJ\nU1RfJB3OEFk93N3L10Y0DZDOjKkQXFYW1gryH8jryHK78nBmBpQ4i3UogO40ey8L\nuclj0I18qgV4JknQ9F7fVSuYRu+H0RCKlMV8l45pMB/jKoYuP4j7fsmQT3Gjn0l+\npUopjCh1Ix4Vhlfu3v8E\n=wK5i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-20T20:07:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","grav