ions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/02200bc9d80931861fdf72b5b7542a17911199a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:36:55Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:36:55Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"chore(submodule): context-vigilance-kit leaves ai-labs as context-v-corpus\n\nThe context-vigilance-kit repo was renamed context-v-corpus and remounted\nat the anchor monorepo root. It collates context-v from the whole tree, so\nit never belonged to one child. Its old seat here is reserved for a fresh,\nlean context-vigilance-kit: the installable cv plugin, which must not drag\nthe corpus''s history into every adopter''s clone.\n\nThis commit removes the submodule. The new kit is mounted once its GitHub\nrepo exists, which waits until every old clone is re-pointed at the\nrenamed URL. Until then, GitHub redirects the old name to the corpus.\n\nFiles changed:\n- .gitmodules, context-vigilance-kit (gitlink removed)\n- CLAUDE.md: children table, ingest path, see-also, rollout-draft path\n- README.md: the kit section now describes the plugin, with a pointer to the corpus\n- .mcp.json: Chroma data-dir now ../context-v-corpus/.chroma\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"62f80240a99a2e40b88b98d2a44184b7bac2f10f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/62f80240a99a2e40b88b98d2a44184b7bac2f10f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/02200bc9d80931861fdf72b5b7542a17911199a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/02200bc9d80931861fdf72b5b7542a17911199a6","node_id":"C_kwDOOMvWKtoAKDAyMjAwYmM5ZDgwOTMxODYxZmRmNzJiNWI3NTQyYTE3OTExMTk5YTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/cfb261d2fc57a68e6d2ae16b993350e32ab80d61","sha":"cfb261d2fc57a68e6d2ae16b993350e32ab80d61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/cfb261d2fc57a68e6d2ae16b993350e32ab80d61"}],"sha":"02200bc9d80931861fdf72b5b7542a17911199a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/02200bc9d80931861fdf72b5b7542a17911199a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/cfb261d2fc57a68e6d2ae16b993350e32ab80d61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T16:50:50Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T16:50:50Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"chore(submodule): bump augment-it — the federated design system arc\n\n145 commits, 5c00a54 -> 380d72b.\n\nSix federal primitives shipped and swept across the federation: Button (285 call\nsites, 19 units), Chip (99/12), CardRow (50/16), ListContainer (32/8),\nStatusIndicator (16/15), CountBadge (11/4), plus three SelectWrapper variants, two\nSelectors, MenuItem and DisclosureRow. 523 call sites total, up from zero.\n\nAlso in the arc: the federal primitives gallery, a type scale and an info tone\nthat DESIGN.md had specified and never shipped, a Tier 1 palette collision where\ntwo named steps shared one hex, `pnpm verify` so a broken member can be named\nrather than hunted, `pnpm organ:census` because the BEM rollup could not see its\nown call sites, and the federation''s first component tests — 64 of them.\n\nDeclared deviations went from 8 to 1. The one that remains is real.\n\nOnly augment-it is bumped. memopop-ai''s pointer also moved and is not this\nsession''s work; context-vigilance-kit and dididecks-ai carry untracked content\nrather than pointer moves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b65787e875a92bc3e10a6e9ab05de3803f13333b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/b65787e875a92bc3e10a6e9ab05de3803f13333b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/cfb261d2fc57a68e6d2ae16b993350e32ab80d61","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/cfb261d2fc57a68e6d2ae16b993350e32ab80d61","node_id":"C_kwDOOMvWKtoAKGNmYjI2MWQyZmM1N2E2OGU2ZDJhZTE2Yjk5MzM1MGUzMmFiODBkNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/e6bea06b659ba4a02a245ffdfe05e4e52681ea28","sha":"e6bea06b659ba4a02a245ffdfe05e4e52681ea28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/e6bea06b659ba4a02a245ffdfe05e4e52681ea28"}],"sha":"cfb261d2fc57a68e6d2ae16b993350e32ab80d61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/cfb261d2fc57a68e6d2ae16b993350e32ab80d61"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/e6bea06b659ba4a02a245ffdfe05e4e52681ea28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:03:16Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:03:16Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"new(study): frontend UI kits and component libraries, ten references pinned\n\nSubmodules the study repo at studies/frontend-ui-kits-component-libraries. It was\nstaged during the design-system work and deliberately left uncommitted — the\nstudy-repos-first skill says to stage a submodule addition and let the operator\nreview before it lands.\n\nThe question it exists to answer: what naming and sizing conventions have the\nmature UI kits converged on, and which of them should augment-it''s component API\nadopt rather than reinvent? The answer shaped the API directly — variant and size\nas two enums, the shadcn variant vocabulary (primary / secondary / outline / ghost\n/ destructive / link), and Tailwind''s `token/N` convention for the rung-3 radius\nmodifier.\n\nThe reason to pin rather than paraphrase is the whole point of a study: foundation\nmodels already know these kits, which makes them very easy to half-remember.\nPinned SHAs mean what we read today is what someone reads in a month.\n\nTen references, each at a fixed SHA: shadcn-ui and shadcn-svelte, radix-primitives,\nbits-ui and melt-ui for the Svelte-native headless lineage, material-ui,\nant-design, tailwindcss, open-props, and primer-primitives. Carbon is covered in\nthe README as a web-studied reference rather than a submodule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"74121f42e21e1110c21e206d26f7e62b864826f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/74121f42e21e1110c21e206d26f7e62b864826f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/e6bea06b659ba4a02a245ffdfe05e4e52681ea28","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/e6bea06b659ba4a02a245ffdfe05e4e52681ea28","node_id":"C_kwDOOMvWKtoAKGU2YmVhMDZiNjU5YmE0YTAyYTI0NWZmZGZlMDVlNGU1MjY4MWVhMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/4f500a886d9a3cbb92f0e8731fb8179e6d7983e3","sha":"4f500a886d9a3cbb92f0e8731fb8179e6d7983e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/4f500a886d9a3cbb92f0e8731fb8179e6d7983e3"}],"sha":"e6bea06b659ba4a02a245ffdfe05e4e52681ea28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/e6bea06b659ba4a02a245ffdfe05e4e52681ea28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/4f500a886d9a3cbb92f0e8731fb8179e6d7983e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T06:59:43Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T06:59:43Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"chore(submodule): bump augment-it, context-vigilance-kit, corpora-builder, dididecks-ai, id-didi-sh\n\nWrap-up pointer bump after a session that moved augment-it substantially. Every\nrecorded HEAD was verified present on its own remote first, so a fresh clone or a\n`git submodule update --init` on another machine resolves all of them.\n\naugment-it carries the day''s work: the counted gap audit against the three\npractices we recommend to clients, the doctrine blueprint developed from a dormant\n2026-06-01 stub, two remediation plans, two loops, the first Archify diagram, the\nsecond Graphify build with its diff against August, and two changelog entries.\n\nThe other four are pointer catch-up from prior sessions, recorded here rather than\nleft dirty across another day.\n\nmemopop-ai is deliberately NOT bumped. Its HEAD f9d95dd exists on no remote, so\nrecording it would hand every other machine a gitlink it cannot resolve. It stays\ndirty until that commit is pushed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014YKv2yY7sAR8z4sQ3KEhet","tree":{"sha":"169b4ad13dc3a5a058a2e6cedfa05ec0386836ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/169b4ad13dc3a5a058a2e6cedfa05ec0386836ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/4f500a886d9a3cbb92f0e8731fb8179e6d7983e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/4f500a886d9a3cbb92f0e8731fb8179e6d7983e3","node_id":"C_kwDOOMvWKtoAKDRmNTAwYTg4NmQ5YTNjYmI5MmYwZTg3MzFmYjgxNzllNmQ3OTgzZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/7010415ec8a6ae9f1ed95924a9da858ea68a23e0","sha":"7010415ec8a6ae9f1ed95924a9da858ea68a23e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/7010415ec8a6ae9f1ed95924a9da858ea68a23e0"}],"sha":"4f500a886d9a3cbb92f0e8731fb8179e6d7983e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/4f500a886d9a3cbb92f0e8731fb8179e6d7983e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/7010415ec8a6ae9f1ed95924a9da858ea68a23e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T16:13:55Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T16:13:55Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"spec(entities): confirm entities.slug.cascade is derived, not a column\n\nOperator confirmed the reading, so the section no longer asks to be\ncorrected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BocV5c3MSp3o7Zo4DyXrz5","tree":{"sha":"5a1e7df9c90418893844532d78d9dc3470609d6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/5a1e7df9c90418893844532d78d9dc3470609d6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/7010415ec8a6ae9f1ed95924a9da858ea68a23e0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/7010415ec8a6ae9f1ed95924a9da858ea68a23e0","node_id":"C_kwDOOMvWKtoAKDcwMTA0MTVlYzhhNmFlOWYxZWQ5NTkyNGE5ZGE4NThlYTY4YTIzZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/5dd6cde96e79f5bb116e53e0f8c9d03b9d11b4ca","sha":"5dd6cde96e79f5bb116e53e0f8c9d03b9d11b4ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/5dd6cde96e79f5bb116e53e0f8c9d03b9d11b4ca"}],"sha":"7010415ec8a6ae9f1ed95924a9da858ea68a23e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/7010415ec8a6ae9f1ed95924a9da858ea68a23e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/5dd6cde96e79f5bb116e53e0f8c9d03b9d11b4ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T16:13:37Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T16:13:37Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"spec(entities): the cascade is invoked, not stored — and the table is entities\n\nTwo operator rulings, recorded together because the second explains the\nfirst.\n\nThe schema question is answered: one `entities` table, `entities.slug` as\nthe identity. `organizations` and `workspaces` reconcile toward it rather\nthan standing beside it, and the email domain becomes a nullable\nself-signup hint. The four to create are [reach-edu], [humain-vc],\n[palmer-ai], [nextladder].\n\nAnd the cascade is a property of the REFERENCE, not of the record. An\nentity named by its slug alone is independent — no parent, no children,\nnothing inherited, which is Ruling 1 unchanged. A chained reference,\n`organization:palmer-ai:workspace:q3-planning`, is a different act:\nwriting the chain is the declaration, and it is what authorises\nparent-child behaviour in the UX and in how data is transformed and\nfetched. Chain it and you get the behaviour; name it alone and you do not.\nNothing about the stored record differs between the two.\n\nThat is what makes Ruling 1 and cascading co-exist rather than compete,\nand it is the shape the retraction was reaching for: a workspace is\ngenuinely shared, so q3-planning may be invoked under Palmer AI on Monday\nand under a joint venture on Tuesday, and neither invocation is more true\nthan the other. Store the parenthood and you must pick one and fight the\nschema for the second. Declare it per reference and both are cheap.\n\nIt also explains why folder nesting has never needed enforcing anywhere in\nthis tree: a path IS a written chain, so it already cascades, and a prefix\ntest is what honouring one looks like.\n\nFlagged: `entities.slug.cascade` is read here as the derived chained form\nbuilt at call time rather than a stored column, consistent with the\nstanding ruling that the colon tuple must not be persisted because the\ncopies would disagree. The section says so and asks to be corrected if a\ncolumn was meant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BocV5c3MSp3o7Zo4DyXrz5","tree":{"sha":"a31fa5331151794f6a25510531bba1293219931a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/a31fa5331151794f6a25510531bba1293219931a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/5dd6cde96e79f5bb116e53e0f8c9d03b9d11b4ca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/5dd6cde96e79f5bb116e53e0f8c9d03b9d11b4ca","node_id":"C_kwDOOMvWKtoAKDVkZDZjZGU5NmU3OWY1YmIxMTZlNTNlMGY4YzlkMDNiOWQxMWI0Y2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/300d20a0657c8717714cb666a3a21b65416e866c","sha":"300d20a0657c8717714cb666a3a21b65416e866c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/300d20a0657c8717714cb666a3a21b65416e866c"}],"sha":"5dd6cde96e79f5bb116e53e0f8c9d03b9d11b4ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/5dd6cde96e79f5bb116e53e0f8c9d03b9d11b4ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/300d20a0657c8717714cb666a3a21b65416e866c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T16:12:12Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T16:12:12Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"spec(entities): cascade is declared propagation — one concept, two applications\n\nCorrects the note added earlier today, which called the credential cascade\nand the tag-syntax cascade a collision and proposed renaming one of them.\nThey are the same idea, and the rename would have cost the unity.\n\nA cascade is declared propagation, not structural inheritance. Someone\nasserts a relationship — by lending to a named set of entities, or by\nnaming a chain — and what follows flows along it. What makes it a cascade\nrather than inheritance is that no stored structure decides it, which is\nwhy it sits beside Ruling 1 rather than against it: hierarchy is not in\ncode, but propagation is still declarable. The colon chain is the\ndeclaring act for naming; cascade_id is the declaring act for authority.\n\nThe credential sense is the EXTENDED one. It carries a cap, a wind-down,\nand an end that pulls every loan at once, because authority needs those\nand a name does not. The syntax sense is the plainer general case. Both\nkeep the same contrast with Okta: there the directory decides what flows,\nhere a person does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BocV5c3MSp3o7Zo4DyXrz5","tree":{"sha":"2c528ea37cc2d2c3bcab7f78664fe121ccad24a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/2c528ea37cc2d2c3bcab7f78664fe121ccad24a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/300d20a0657c8717714cb666a3a21b65416e866c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/300d20a0657c8717714cb666a3a21b65416e866c","node_id":"C_kwDOOMvWKtoAKDMwMGQyMGEwNjU3Yzg3MTc3MTRjYjY2NmEzYTIxYjY1NDE2ZTg2NmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/cc1925a454775b317892265ca7a32010113359a4","sha":"cc1925a454775b317892265ca7a32010113359a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/cc1925a454775b317892265ca7a32010113359a4"}],"sha":"300d20a0657c8717714cb666a3a21b65416e866c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/300d20a0657c8717714cb666a3a21b65416e866c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/cc1925a454775b317892265ca7a32010113359a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T16:10:00Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T16:10:00Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"spec(didi): the handle is the identity, and a session holds several entities\n\nEvolved thinking from the corpora-builder side, propagated back to the\ncanonical spec and the 2026-08-08 plan rather than left to diverge.\n\nRuling 4 kept organizations as domain-as-id. That cannot hold for the same\nreason ruling 2 exists: `palmer-ai` is not an email domain and the account\nwas made on a human.vc address, so an org keyed on a domain it does not\nown has to be faked before it can be created. `organizations.slug` already\nexists and is the handle; it becomes the identity and `domain` becomes a\nnullable self-signup hint, exactly as `default_domain` already is on the\nworkspace. One argument, applied twice.\n\nNextLadder is recorded as the worked case for an entity with no corpus, no\nbucket and no domain — an org somebody belongs to before anything has been\nprovisioned. Any code assuming entity implies storage breaks on the first\none, so entity creation and resource provisioning stay separate steps.\n\nThe workspace picker was single-select. It becomes a set: a person\nconsulting across several organizations holds them open at once, and the\ncorpora are expected to overlap massively on purpose. Two consequences\nthat bind every consumer — read is the union but WRITE NAMES EXACTLY ONE,\nbecause with three tenants open \"file this\" has no safe default and\ninferring one puts a client''s material in another client''s corpus; and the\nbrokered credentials become a per-tenant map with independent expiries\nrather than a single credential.\n\nNamed as blocking: Flexible-Entity-Relationships Ruling 1 specifies one\nentities table with kind as a display label and no parent_id, having\nexplicitly retracted containment, while the identity spec still specifies\nseparate organizations and workspaces with org_id. Both cannot be built,\nand creating the four entities requires choosing. The newer ruling is the\nbetter-argued one — projects are collaborations among many organizations —\nbut it is an operator call.\n\nAlso flags a terminology collision in Flexible-Entity-Relationships:\n\"cascade\" there is a lender''s declared act across entities and explicitly\nNOT structural, while the tag syntax now uses it to mean a chain composing\nthrough levels. One of them has to be renamed before either is coded.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BocV5c3MSp3o7Zo4DyXrz5","tree":{"sha":"1481ff38069d46cb2263318653df64489a8659f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/1481ff38069d46cb2263318653df64489a8659f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/cc1925a454775b317892265ca7a32010113359a4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/cc1925a454775b317892265ca7a32010113359a4","node_id":"C_kwDOOMvWKtoAKGNjMTkyNWE0NTQ3NzViMzE3ODkyMjY1Y2E3YTMyMDEwMTEzMzU5YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/d544c933ecdc8cdc93ed92c91bbe04e29a4ffe1a","sha":"d544c933ecdc8cdc93ed92c91bbe04e29a4ffe1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/d544c933ecdc8cdc93ed92c91bbe04e29a4ffe1a"}],"sha":"cc1925a454775b317892265ca7a32010113359a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/cc1925a454775b317892265ca7a32010113359a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/d544c933ecdc8cdc93ed92c91bbe04e29a4ffe1a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T05:52:52Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T05:52:52Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"plan(didi): agent chat asks the R2 credential question again\n\nAdditive revision — 75 insertions, 6 deletions, and every deletion is a line\nre-emitted: the two revision dates, the semantic version, the summary''s phase\nrange, and one open question renumbered 3 to 4 with its text untouched.\n\nFrom the operator''s question: can in-app agent chat just interface with Claude\nCode on this machine instead of using tokens?\n\nTechnically yes — Agent SDK picking up the CLI''s credentials, `claude -p`\nheadless, or inverting it entirely and exposing corpora-builder as an MCP server.\nThe sidecar already spawns processes, so the first two are a module rather than\nan architecture.\n\nThe reason it belongs in THIS plan is that \"instead of using tokens\" is not what\nhappens. Tokens are still spent, against a subscription rather than API credits —\nand using your own seat for your own tooling is a different thing from shipping\nan app whose client installs drive that seat. Which is Open Question 1 with one\nnoun changed: does a client machine hold an R2 credential, or call something that\nreads on its behalf, becomes does it hold a MODEL credential or call something\nthat infers on its behalf.\n\ndidi.sh already has the mechanism. `credential_controller.lend/2` lends a\ncredential to an entity, and an Anthropic key is not structurally different from\nan R2 key. So the answer is a sequence rather than a product choice: MCP now\nbecause it needs no identity at all, in-app chat after Phase D because that is\nwhere \"which credential does this entity infer with\" gets somewhere to live, and\nread the terms before building on subscription auth because that is a licensing\nquestion that gets an account flagged rather than erroring.\n\nTwo smaller notes recorded: the `claude` CLI cannot be assumed present on a\ncollaborator''s machine, which adds to Phase E''s install surface; and `viewer`\ngains a third possible meaning — can they spend inference — which is plausibly\nthe sharpest of the three because it is the one with a bill attached.\n\nPhase F sketched, deliberately last: everything above it is about knowing who is\nasking, and a chat surface that cannot answer that cannot be given to a client.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BocV5c3MSp3o7Zo4DyXrz5","tree":{"sha":"bf1296dd078454689ab509172e284ca2ff7d66c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/bf1296dd078454689ab509172e284ca2ff7d66c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/d544c933ecdc8cdc93ed92c91bbe04e29a4ffe1a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/d544c933ecdc8cdc93ed92c91bbe04e29a4ffe1a","node_id":"C_kwDOOMvWKtoAKGQ1NDRjOTMzZWNkYzhjZGM5M2VkOTJjOTFiYmUwNGUyOWE0ZmZlMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/6bb2cc6dde1a90f5ad93f2e945b34bc33c81f056","sha":"6bb2cc6dde1a90f5ad93f2e945b34bc33c81f056","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/6bb2cc6dde1a90f5ad93f2e945b34bc33c81f056"}],"sha":"d544c933ecdc8cdc93ed92c91bbe04e29a4ffe1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/d544c933ecdc8cdc93ed92c91bbe04e29a4ffe1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/6bb2cc6dde1a90f5ad93f2e945b34bc33c81f056/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T04:11:25Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T04:11:25Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"add(blueprints): show the filesystem of a workspace\n\nExtracted from the two ai-labs surfaces that now show a workspace tree —\nflave-ai''s editor over a real disk, corpora-builder''s Files tab over an R2 object\nstore. They agree about almost everything, and the one place they disagree is\nwhere the actual decision lives, which is what made the pattern worth writing\ndown rather than copying twice more.\n\nFive decisions codified: the four-field node shape (plus `count` once a folder\nhas 66 children); paths workspace-relative and ASSERTED even where the language\nmakes escape hard; folders-first-then-plain-alphabetical, with the warning that a\ncleverer tiebreak reads as random; hide the app''s business but show the user''s —\nwith the sharper test being \"does this level tell the reader anything\" rather\nthan \"is this internal\"; and write the backend seam before the second backend\nexists, which flave-ai''s own comment argues is the only time it is cheap.\n\nPlus the three traps neither implementation could have predicted from the markup:\ntree rows must opt OUT of a global control primitive or 944 of them inherit a\nborder and a field background; --depth is a legitimate component-local property\nand a drift checker that rejects it is wrong; and when you flatten a level for\ndisplay, flatten what you draw and never what you hand back.\n\nThe store-backed section is the real adaptation. An object store has no\ndirectories, so the tree is derived from keys — which is better than walking a\ndisk, measurably: the same derivation done by reading files cost 20.6 seconds\nagainst R2 and presented as a hung window. The promise is asserted as reads == 0,\nnot as elapsed time.\n\nEnds with a checklist for the third implementation, since dididecks and\naugment-it both sit on folders their users cannot see.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BocV5c3MSp3o7Zo4DyXrz5","tree":{"sha":"a912a820b1759fb82cb0a9798ae86bb4005fb70a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/a912a820b1759fb82cb0a9798ae86bb4005fb70a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/6bb2cc6dde1a90f5ad93f2e945b34bc33c81f056","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/6bb2cc6dde1a90f5ad93f2e945b34bc33c81f056","node_id":"C_kwDOOMvWKtoAKDZiYjJjYzZkZGUxYTkwZjVhZDkzZjJlOTQ1YjM0YmMzM2M4MWYwNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/b22e7e321be99bcc2cf27aad46f6bda0c2b18efe","sha":"b22e7e321be99bcc2cf27aad46f6bda0c2b18efe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/b22e7e321be99bcc2cf27aad46f6bda0c2b18efe"}],"sha":"6bb2cc6dde1a90f5ad93f2e945b34bc33c81f056","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/6bb2cc6dde1a90f5ad93f2e945b34bc33c81f056"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/b22e7e321be99bcc2cf27aad46f6bda0c2b18efe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:25:00Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:25:00Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"add(reminders): load the theme system before touching tokens\n\nWritten after building corpora-builder''s theme twice from the wrong source. The\nreminder carries the three things that were actually wrong, so the next session\ndoes not rediscover them:\n\n1. The house convention is theme-system + the astro-knots blueprint, not\n   augment-it''s DESIGN.md — which is an elaboration of it, with federation\n   vocabulary layered on top. Three layers, two tiers, --fx-* as semantic tier,\n   data-theme and data-mode as SEPARATE axes, three modes with vibrant\n   dark-based, descriptive font roles.\n2. memopop-ai/packages/shared-styles is not the family brand. Nothing renders\n   it. Both live surfaces are violet-magenta; source colour from augment-it.\n   And converging the didi.sh brand onto that palette is separate, deliberate\n   work — which is what the data-theme axis exists to keep possible.\n3. A rename changes nothing visible and must not be reported as convergence.\n\nPlus the practice that would have caught all of it sooner: render headless\nagainst a fixture harness before claiming anything about how something looks.\nThat is how graphite-800 == graphite-700 surfaced — augment-it''s open gate A22,\nwhich makes every card border paint nothing in dark, and which three careful\nreadings of the CSS missed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BocV5c3MSp3o7Zo4DyXrz5","tree":{"sha":"8cdd11950da1658bf057e52b30d99f