,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/35aa18ffba972287bc869d28b7c2046e0a9ef7c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-14T01:07:01Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-14T01:07:01Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"chore(submodules): promote agent-harnesses and conversational-ui-and-native-shells to standalone study repos\n\nBoth new studies had grown past the study-repos-first \"more than four or\nfive references\" promotion threshold (10 and 8 repos respectively) but\nwere registered as flat per-repo gitlinks directly in ai-labs/.gitmodules,\nunlike the existing memory-layers-for-agents and open-specs-and-standards\nstudies, which are each a single submodule pointing at their own\nlossless-group/study-<slug> repo.\n\nFixes that inconsistency. Removed the ten agent-harnesses and eight\nconversational-ui-and-native-shells reference-repo gitlinks (plus each\nstudy''s loose README/context-v) from ai-labs directly, and re-added each\nstudy as a single submodule pointing at its new standalone repo\n(lossless-group/study-agent-harnesses, lossless-group/study-conversational-ui-and-native-shells).\nContent is unchanged — same ten and eight reference repos pinned at the\nsame commits, same profiles and inquiry docs, just nested one level\ndeeper per convention.","tree":{"sha":"1f8f19d7b2d07809e1630abee0e691b77e7171ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/1f8f19d7b2d07809e1630abee0e691b77e7171ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/35aa18ffba972287bc869d28b7c2046e0a9ef7c1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/35aa18ffba972287bc869d28b7c2046e0a9ef7c1","node_id":"C_kwDOOMvWKtoAKDM1YWExOGZmYmE5NzIyODdiYzg2OWQyOGI3YzIwNDZlMGE5ZWY3YzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commit/f4dc2d27781a7e01c85a396ad221e0f0e9331ca4","sha":"f4dc2d27781a7e01c85a396ad221e0f0e9331ca4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/f4dc2d27781a7e01c85a396ad221e0f0e9331ca4"}],"sha":"35aa18ffba972287bc869d28b7c2046e0a9ef7c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/35aa18ffba972287bc869d28b7c2046e0a9ef7c1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/commits/f4dc2d27781a7e01c85a396ad221e0f0e9331ca4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T22:45:53Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T22:45:53Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"new(agent-harnesses, conversational-ui-and-native-shells): pin two studies for the cross-product native agent shell decision\n\nWe want a native, cross-platform chat app that can swap between augment-it,\ndididecks-ai, and memopop-ai backends at runtime, dynamically loading and\nunloading skills and MCP servers per context. Before designing that, we\nstudied how real agent harnesses and native conversational UIs actually\nsolve this — grounded in pinned source, not training-data folklore, per\nthe study-repos-first convention.\n\nTwo new studies land under studies/: agent-harnesses/ (10 repos — opencode,\ngoose, aider, OpenHands, mcp-python-sdk, continue, autogen, cline, codex,\npi) covers how coding-agent runtimes organize files, persist memory, trace\ntool calls, scope MCP/tools, and load skills. conversational-ui-and-native-shells/\n(8 repos — Kaas, openagent, Dive, 5ire, anything-llm, routa, open-vibe,\nlibrechat) covers how native Tauri-first chat apps handle state, multi-\ncontext switching, local persistence, and MCP-client integration. Every\nrepo has a deep Profile__<Name>.md grounded in real file:line citations\nfrom the actual pinned checkout, plus two inquiry docs answering the\nstudy plan''s targeted questions.\n\nTwo supporting docs at the ai-labs context-v level: an internal audit\n(In-App-Agent-Chat-As-Built-vs-As-Specced.md) correcting an assumption\nabout the existing 2026-05-18 in-app-agent architecture docs — augment-it''s\nchat does follow the workspace/chat split those docs specced, it just\nnever got extracted into the shared @lossless/in-app-agent package. And\nthe actual decision doc (Cross-Product-Native-Agent-Shell.md), which\nrecommends extending memopop-native (proven Tauri + Rust sidecar-dispatcher\nsubstrate) rather than building a standalone app, using routa''s confirmed\ngenuine per-session process-level adapter swap as the reference\narchitecture and anything-llm''s confirmed shallow workspace-switching as\nthe negative example to avoid.\n\nThe plan this all serves lives at\ncontext-v/plans/Study-Agent-Harnesses-and-Conversational-UI-Before-Cross-Product-Shell.md.\n\nAlso included:\n- studies/README.md index updated with both new entries","tree":{"sha":"8293560bc7efe22d649ba3a90891499bcb43f7ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/trees/8293560bc7efe22d649ba3a90891499bcb43f7ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/lossless-ai-labs/git/commits/f4dc2d27781a7e01c85a396ad221e0f0e9331ca4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admi