ommits/f1b38bb2e2df51dade40618cab070175a3abd6a5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/20m61/v1z3r/commits/1e54b91545ffaea4563e1cc4a15bf9581c33f644/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-07-20T01:16:29Z","email":"bot@v1z3r.com","name":"V1Z3R Bot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-07-20T01:16:29Z","email":"bot@v1z3r.com","name":"V1Z3R Bot"},"message":"feat: Add comprehensive performance monitoring and error tracking\n\n## Summary\n- Enhanced performance monitoring for WebGL/WebGPU fallback scenarios\n- Improved ErrorBoundary with detailed error context and tracking\n- Created PerformanceDashboard component for real-time monitoring\n- Added WebGPU support detection and render mode tracking\n\n## Key Features\n\n### Performance Monitoring Enhancements\n- WebGPU support detection and initialization timing\n- Render mode tracking (WebGPU/WebGL/fallback)\n- Texture upload performance monitoring\n- Particle count tracking with performance warnings\n- Shader compilation time measurement\n\n### Error Tracking Integration\n- Enhanced ErrorBoundary with performance context\n- Error metrics collection and storage\n- RUM endpoint integration for error reporting\n- Session storage for local error debugging\n\n### Monitoring Dashboard\n- Real-time performance metrics display\n- Compact and detailed view modes\n- Error history visualization\n- Performance budget violation alerts\n- Render mode usage statistics\n\n### Developer Experience\n- Debug mode for detailed logging\n- Performance thresholds and warnings\n- Memory usage tracking\n- Frame rate monitoring with status indicators\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aee0d0e78151a9c453cf8fdcce8200056764af1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/20m61/v1z3r/git/trees/aee0d0e78151a9c453cf8fdcce8200056764af1b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/20m61/v1z3r/git/commits/1e54b91545ffaea4563e1cc4a15bf9581c33f644","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/20m61/v1z3r/commit/1e54b91545ffaea4563e1cc4a15bf9581c33f644","node_id":"C_kwDOOM6kQ9oAKDFlNTRiOTE1NDVmZmFlYTQ1NjNlMWNjNGExNWJmOTU4MWMzM2Y2NDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/20m61/v1z3r/commit/4b8f65b940c0836f67fc63dbeabd152c778cdc91","sha":"4b8f65b940c0836f67fc63dbeabd152c778cdc91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/20m61/v1z3r/commits/4b8f65b940c0836f67fc63dbeabd152c778cdc91"}],"sha":"1e54b91545ffaea4563e1cc4a15bf9581c33f644","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/20m61/v1z3r/commits/1e54b91545ffaea4563e1cc4a15bf9581c33f644"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1693436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20m61/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20m61/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20m61/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20m61/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/20m61","id":1693436,"login":"20m61","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTM0MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20m61/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20m61/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20m61/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20m61/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/20m61/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/20m61","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/20m61/v1z3r/commits/4b8f65b940c0836f67fc63dbeabd152c778cdc91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-07-20T00:47:35Z","email":"ifm0s1m0s1m0nn@hotmail.com","name":"20m61"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-07-20T00:47:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Add static export compatibility and improve error handling (#37)\n\n* feat: Add static export compatibility and improve error handling\n\n## Summary\n- Add VJApplicationWrapper for proper SSR/static export hydration\n- Implement comprehensive ErrorBoundary component with fallback UI\n- Create SafeWebGPUVisualizer with graceful WebGL fallback\n- Remove framer-motion dependency for static export compatibility\n- Add stable ID generator to prevent hydration mismatches\n- Improve global error handling in _app.tsx\n- Add environment configuration utility\n- Simplify Lambda preset handler for testing\n\n## Key Changes\n\n### Frontend Improvements\n- **VJApplicationWrapper**: Lazy loads VJApplication to avoid SSR issues\n- **ErrorBoundary**: Catches React errors with user-friendly recovery options\n- **SafeWebGPUVisualizer**: Provides WebGL fallback when WebGPU unavailable\n- **WebGPUVisualizer**: Dynamic imports and proper WebGPU detection\n- **ID Generator**: Stable IDs across server/client for hydration\n- **Global Error Handling**: Enhanced error capture in _app.tsx\n\n### Infrastructure Updates\n- Simplified Lambda preset handler (index-simple.js) for testing\n- Updated CDK dependencies and configurations\n- Improved error logging across Lambda functions\n\n### Static Export Compatibility\n- Removed framer-motion AnimatePresence for CSS-based animations\n- Fixed Date.now() hydration mismatches\n- Added proper window/process checks for SSR safety\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Address review feedback - improve type safety and remove emojis\n\n- Fix env.ts to remove non-existent window.process reference\n- Remove emoji from ErrorBoundary component (per project guidelines)\n- Add proper TypeScript interfaces for WebGPU/AI components\n- Fix all type errors with proper type guards and optional chaining\n- Add audioData prop to WebGPUVisualizer component\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: V1Z3R Bot <bot@v1z3r.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"12cb38bdf0ce6892a1a678f251b3d2654fbf942d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/20m61/v1z3r/git/trees/12cb38bdf0ce6892a1a678f251b3d2654fbf942d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/20m61/v1z3r/git/commits/4b8f65b940c0836f67fc63dbeabd152c778cdc91","verification":{"payload":"tree 12cb38bdf0ce6892a1a678f251b3d2654fbf942d\nparent 7f664a26216c074cdd225435379e26b99163de7b\nauthor 20m61 <ifm0s1m0s1m0nn@hotmail.com> 1752972455 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1752972455 +0900\n\nfeat: Add static export compatibility and improve error handling (#37)\n\n* feat: Add static export compatibility and improve error handling\n\n## Summary\n- Add VJApplicationWrapper for proper SSR/static export hydration\n- Implement comprehensive ErrorBoundary component with fallback UI\n- Create SafeWebGPUVisualizer with graceful WebGL fallback\n- Remove framer-motion dependency for static export compatibility\n- Add stable ID generator to prevent hydration mismatches\n- Improve global error handling in _app.tsx\n- Add environment configuration utility\n- Simplify Lambda preset handler for testing\n\n## Key Changes\n\n### Frontend Improvements\n- **VJApplicationWrapper**: Lazy loads VJApplication to avoid SSR issues\n- **ErrorBoundary**: Catches React errors with user-friendly recovery options\n- **SafeWebGPUVisualizer**: Provides WebGL fallback when WebGPU unavailable\n- **WebGPUVisualizer**: Dynamic imports and proper WebGPU detection\n- **ID Generator**: Stable IDs across server/client for hydration\n- **Global Error Handling**: Enhanced error capture in _app.tsx\n\n### Infrastructure Updates\n- Simplified Lambda preset handler (index-simple.js) for testing\n- Updated CDK dependencies and configurations\n- Improved error logging across Lambda functions\n\n### Static Export Compatibility\n- Removed framer-motion AnimatePresence for CSS-based an